# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored `MANIFEST` matches at ANY depth,
# and because Windows git runs with core.ignorecase=true it also matched the directory
# `ingest/manifest/` — silently excluding the corpus source-of-truth manifests from
# every commit. That is why they were missing after a machine change (see
# docs/PAPER_WORKLOG.md, 2026-09-17). setuptools only ever writes MANIFEST at the root.
/MANIFEST

# Corpus provenance — these define which documents make up the corpus and must always
# be committed. Explicit re-include, so no future ignore rule can swallow them again.
!ingest/manifest/
!ingest/manifest/**

